WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:04.210
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
they screened the first episode of The Flash

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:05.210
at Comic Con, Legally.

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.120
So this is going to be my non-spoilery review.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.120
Since a lot of you probably won’t get to
see it until October 7th when it officially

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.120
premieres, I’m going to do no-spoilers first,
then for everyone that has already seen it,

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.690
I will have a spoiler section with a special
warning.

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:15.960
Hello any new people too, if you’re just
finding me I do weekly Flash and Arrow videos,

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:17.010
be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.410
I’ve got a special Flash and Arrow Comic
Con Giveaway and I’ll explain what’s going

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:22.460
on with those panels because I will be uploading
them.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:23.460
Flash Review first.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.580
I feel like because of what this show is,
the cast they picked and the creative team

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.480
behind it, the trailers they’ve posted tell
you everything up front.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:35.620
So watching the actual episode doesn’t reveal
anything comic book readers or Arrow fans

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:36.620
didn’t already know.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:40.940
It’s through and through all the best stuff
from Arrow, but done in the light of day with

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:41.940
more humor.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:45.580
That’s because Barry Allen is much more
positive than Oliver Queen.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:50.390
If you saw Grant Gustin on Arrow, his portrayal
of Barry is virtually unchanged.

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:52.450
They haven’t messed with the character or
anything.

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:56.700
It’s a direct continuation and because so
much time has passed, they deal with those

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.930
time gaps in very creative ways.

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:02.489
If you haven’t see Arrow before then all
I can say is that Grant Gustin has the perfect

00:01:02.489 --> 00:01:03.550
kind of energy for The Flash.

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:08.470
He’s like this hyper-curious best friend
type that makes you feel like he’ll definitely

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:10.280
be Justice League material some day.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.590
This show is all about his origin story.

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:16.320
So give him a few years to get the moves down
and he’ll be running laps around Superman

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.320
in no time.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:20.390
Just to clarify, I’m not talking about Grant
Gustin being in Justice League, I’m talking

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:22.860
about the comic book version of the Flash
joining the Justice League.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:25.870
He’s an A List member, top tier level powers.

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:30.240
When he’s able to draw enough energy from
the Speed Force he can run so fast he travels

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.240
forward and backward in time.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:34.560
Time Travel powers combined with the ability
to outrun Superman automatically make you

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.090
an A-List superhero.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:39.240
The Flash we meet in the first episode is
just starting to figure things out and put

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.770
his own Team Arrow together.

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:45.690
I guess we can call them Team Flash, all the
supporting characters are great.

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:48.689
Including Detective Pretty Boy played by Rick
Cosnett.

00:01:48.689 --> 00:01:52.630
I feel like because his name is Edward Thawne,
everyone is going to go into the episode with

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:56.170
certain expectations and still come out surprised.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:01.979
The definitely give a hat tip to the name
Thawne and the idea of running fast, but even

00:02:01.979 --> 00:02:04.320
knowing everything I knew before hand.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:08.009
I was still blown away by a few big left turns
in the plot.

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:12.400
Team Flash, what forms initially at least
as Barry’s support circle are already characters

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.370
you’ve met.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:19.191
Tom Cavanagh’s Harrison Wells character
is the person who runs STAR LABS is kind of

00:02:19.191 --> 00:02:20.959
like a parental-type figure.

00:02:20.959 --> 00:02:24.500
Not quite, but on the show he’s too old
to be like a Diggle character.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:27.760
He feels more like a Slade Wilson from Arrow
Season 1.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:30.510
Only in that he’s a mentor.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:33.340
They come together in this really interesting
way.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:38.330
There are a lot of comic book easter eggs
and the show is thus far, the most faithful

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:41.130
comic book adaptation DC has done.

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:43.730
It’s more faithful to the Flash comics than
Arrow is to the comics, just to give you something

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:44.730
to compare it to.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:48.190
The Villain they use to call Barry to Action
is someone you guys will really enjoy.

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:53.360
The way they integrate the Particle Accelerator
Explosion and all the superpowers totally

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.510
worked for me and visually it looked great.

00:02:56.510 --> 00:03:01.740
The big concern with a show like this is the
expense of doing superpowers on screen every

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:02.740
week.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:07.030
During the era of Smallville it would have
cost ten times as much to do what this first

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:08.030
episode does.

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:10.459
And it’s only going to get cheaper as seasons
progress.

00:03:10.459 --> 00:03:14.210
Seriously, I have no doubt that we’ll see
a season 2, I don’t expect them to make

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:18.140
an announcement until after the first couple
of episodes have aired.

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:23.030
But this will be one of the strongest new
shows the CW has.

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:26.550
They’ve already announced several additional
comic book characters coming on the show including

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:30.910
Robbie Amell as Firestorm and now Plastique.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:34.500
If you remember, Arrow took it easy on Comic
Book stuff when it first started.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:37.440
Well the Flash is going full throttle.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.349
And that includes Arrow crossovers.

00:03:40.349 --> 00:03:44.800
Right now the mid season finale of both shows
will be a two hour crossover event.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:47.510
Each shows will have a two parter.

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:53.180
The first part will comprise that two hour
crossover, the second parts will be dealt

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:54.680
with separately when the seasons come back.

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:57.909
That just gets me so pumped for both shows
this fall.

00:03:57.909 --> 00:03:59.670
And yes, I will be doing weekly vids for both
shows.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:00.890
I know a lot of you have been asking.

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:03.790
So now I’m going to talk about some of my
specific favorite moments which means spoilers,

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:06.020
so careful in case you don’t want to know
anything.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:09.980
I’ll wait just a sec...okay, here we go.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:14.159
Amongst many many favorites, I think my biggest
moment of Joy was the Harrison Wells reveal

00:04:14.159 --> 00:04:15.159
at the end.

00:04:15.159 --> 00:04:18.590
Right off the bat I’ll say I’m thinking
the show is going to use him as a Flash, Grant

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:22.990
Gustin of course and Edward Thawne, detective
pretty boy.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:31.639
Here’s the thing, if they’re taking a
lot of plot cues from Flash Rebirth think

00:04:31.639 --> 00:04:35.979
about how Geoff Johns made the transition
from the Eobard Thawne Professor Zoom to the

00:04:35.979 --> 00:04:37.430
next one, Hunter Zolomon.

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:44.930
I think Harrison Wells is either going to
be The Rival inhabiting the body of Max Mercury,

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:49.120
he has the ability to time travel via the
Speed Force which explains the newspaper from

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:53.189
the future or he’s Eobard Thawne, the true
Professor Zoom.

00:04:53.189 --> 00:04:57.219
Regardless of which Reverse Flash he is, I
think Edward Thawne on the show is going to

00:04:57.219 --> 00:04:59.039
become the Hunter Zolomon character.

00:04:59.039 --> 00:05:04.490
They’ll just give him Hunter Zolomon’s
story.

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:09.780
The Gorilla Grodd easter egg was something
the producers had to fight to keep in.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:14.229
Really, the network was going to take it out
but they said it had to stay in just to give

00:05:14.229 --> 00:05:16.069
us that WTF awesome moment.

00:05:16.069 --> 00:05:19.219
I don’t think they’ll use the Grodd character
anytime soon, but he could totally be here

00:05:19.219 --> 00:05:20.219
in season 2.

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:27.699
Think of his story as like a Dawn of the Planet
of the Apes situation.

00:05:27.699 --> 00:05:31.560
As for Team Flash, now that we know Robbie
Amell is playing Caitlin Snow’s supposedly

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:34.199
dead fiancee, Ronnie Raymond aka Firestorm.

00:05:34.199 --> 00:05:38.300
I’m wondering if they’ll still drive her
to the darkside like her comic book persona,

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:39.580
Killer Frost.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:43.830
Something big would have to happen between
her and Firestorm for her to turn on the team.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:46.319
Robbie Amell’s character is debuting in
the fourth episode.

00:05:46.319 --> 00:05:48.439
And yes, they are doing the Martin Stein thing.

00:05:48.439 --> 00:05:51.080
He’s going to be a character on the show
that we’ll meet eventually.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:57.301
No word on what the Firestorm costume will
look like, but expect it to be a slightly

00:05:57.301 --> 00:06:00.589
modified from the comics like Grant Gustin’s
Flash costume.

00:06:00.589 --> 00:06:04.490
They’ll probably dig some Star Labs tech
out to help him contain his Firestorm powers

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:06.849
whenever he activates them.

00:06:06.849 --> 00:06:10.669
That final Future Newspaper everyone has been
freaking out over is what’s going to inform

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:12.289
the major arc of season 1.

00:06:12.289 --> 00:06:16.789
Eventually Team Flash will learn what’s
going on with Harrison Wells, what he’s

00:06:16.789 --> 00:06:17.789
trying to do.

00:06:17.789 --> 00:06:25.659
Here’s a crackpot theory, in the newspaper
it says “Flash Dissappears”, what if he

00:06:25.659 --> 00:06:28.639
dissapeared to the past and Harrison Wells
is really Barry Allen?

00:06:28.639 --> 00:06:31.289
I don’t think that’s the case, mostly
because Harrison Wells had been shown working

00:06:31.289 --> 00:06:35.319
at STAR Labs as a brilliant scientist for
a long period of time.

00:06:35.319 --> 00:06:37.089
Barry Allen is not a brilliant scientist,
he’s clever, but he’s not an expert at

00:06:37.089 --> 00:06:38.139
Theoretical Particle Physics.

00:06:38.139 --> 00:06:39.879
Harrison Wells is someone else.

00:06:39.879 --> 00:06:43.629
But I do think he’s trying to affect a future
outcome by changing the past.

00:06:43.629 --> 00:06:46.749
All Flash stories become Time Travel stories
at a certain point.

00:06:46.749 --> 00:06:53.539
